            <ArticleTitle>[Snapping scapula: the value of 3D imaging].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>379-81</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Snapping scapula is a rare and poorly known cause of shoulder pain and is related to mechanical impingement between the scapula and the rib cage. We present a case in which CT scan was valuable, as a complement to clinical evaluation, for demonstrating the bony component of this entity. 3D reconstructions greatly facilitated diagnosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
